sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7149713-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7149713</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4988662-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4988662</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1199185A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON STEEL CHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI YASUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON STEEL CHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, YASUHISA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI YASUHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, YASUHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermal recording material which has excellent sensitivity in color development and gives an image having excellent storage stability. The recording material comprises a support and formed thereon a thermally color-developing layer comprising a leuco dye which is colorless or light-colored at ordinary temperature, at least one organic acid substance which upon heating reacts with the leuco dye to cause it to develop a color, and a sensitizer. The organic acid substance is at least one diphenyl sulfone derivative selected among 4-hydroxydiphenyl sulfone derivatives represented by general formula (1) or (2), 4,4'-dihydroxydiphenyl sulfone, and 2,4'-dihydroxydiphenyl sulfone, and the sensitizer is a 4-acylbiphenyl. In the formula (1), R1 represents alkyl, aralkyl, or aryl. In the formula (1), Y represents a divalent organic group, and n is an integer of 0 to 6.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un matériau pour thermogravure qui présente une sensibilité excellente s'agissant du développement des couleurs et permet d'obtenir une image dotée d'une excellente stabilité de conservation. Ce matériau pour thermogravure comporte un support recouvert d'une couche pour le développement thermique des couleurs comportant un colorant à base d'un leucodérivé qui est transparent ou peu coloré à température ordinaire, au moins une substance acide organique qui réagit, lorsqu'elle est chauffée, avec le colorant à base de leucodérivé de sorte que celui-ci révèle une couleur, et un sensibilisateur. La substance acide organique est au moins un dérivé diphénylsulfone sélectionné parmi des dérivés de 4-hydroxydiphénylsulfone représentés par une des formules générales (1) ou (2), et une 2,4'-dihydroxydiphénylsulfone, et le sensibilisateur est un 4-acylbiphényle. Dans la formule (1), R1 représente alkyle, aralkyle ou aryle. Dans la formule (2), Y représente un groupe organique divalent et n est un entier compris entre 0 et 6.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>